    },
    "message": "Add state_row! and typed fields, and write the sample namespace with them\n\nField says what a value of a row can do: read itself from Python, go back, write canonical JSON\nand take a forwarded write. state_row! writes all of that from a record's list of fields, plus\nmirrored setters that change the row and the tree together. Any Field is a Row. Tree is what the\nsetters write through, inside with_row_tree: the C API, scalars only, so the node table stays right.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
