    "tree": {
      "sha": "534398712e1f3554c3357661bf34e35e787f0b0d",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jphacks/tkb_2615/git/trees/534398712e1f3554c3357661bf34e35e787f0b0d"
    },
    "message": "Move the long-term distress and the distress monitor to Rust with their namespaces\n\nRust now owns psychological_distress_v1 and metric_state in every world with the kernels on.\nThe end of the update phase is a segment: it plans everything from the rows, says Unsupported for\nanything the Python rules would look at twice, and writes changed values in place, so a tick no\nlonger writes the namespace whole. The Python rules stay as the comparison base and still run for\na tainted namespace, a value the rule turns down, and SHELTERSIM_NATIVE=0. The validator of the\nnamespace moves too. next_long_term_distress is split out of the Python rule, with no change in\nwhat it computes, so the bits can be compared with the kernel's.\n\nbenchmarks/rule_shadow compares the kernel with the Python rules at every call in any process, and\ncounts Unsupported by reason, since hashes pass whether the kernel ran or not. The tracked mirror's\ntest sessions own nothing, and the order reversal of tick_probe goes through dict's own methods.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
